# Rotate an API key

Replace a leaked or expiring API key without downtime.

Rotate keys every *90 days*, or right away if one leaks.

## Prerequisites

Admin access to the console.

> **Warning:** Creating a new key **revokes** the old one immediately. Update these first:
>
> 1. The CI secret
> 2. Local `.env` files

## 1. Open **Settings → API keys**

![Open Settings → API keys](images/01-open-settings-api-keys.png)

## 2. Enter your password to confirm

![Enter your password to confirm](images/02-enter-your-password-to-confirm.png)

Password input is masked while recording.

## 3. Click **Create key** and copy the new key

![Click Create key and copy the new key](images/03-click-create-key-and-copy-the-new-key.png)

The key is shown **once**. Store it in your password manager; see [Managing keys](https://example.com/docs/keys).

> **Decision:** Is the key used in **production**?
>
> - **Yes:** Go to Step 4
> - **No:** Go to Step 5
> - **Unsure:** Go to the guide “Find where an API key is used”

## 4. Drag the new key to **Production**

![Drag the new key to Production](images/04-drag-the-new-key-to-production.png)

## 5. Check that the key works

![Check that the key works](images/05-check-that-the-key-works.png)

Run this in Terminal:

`curl -H "x-api-key: $KEY" https://api.example.com/v1/ping`

It should print *pong*.

